        ":question/id": "27ac3b22-fbfa-5462-a1dd-0b201ecdce85",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int (4\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x-1{csc}^{2}x+7\\operatorname{sin}x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cot}x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}x+C, \\\\ \\int sin x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (4\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x-1{csc}^{2}x+7\\operatorname{sin}x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\,\\text{d}x-1\\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\operatorname{sin}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sec}x-1(-\\operatorname{cot}x)+7(-\\operatorname{cos}x)+C \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sec}x+1\\operatorname{cot}x-7\\operatorname{cos}x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
